    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d354">

                <pb facs="0346" n="336" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg336"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.796/148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Tuck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-07-23T17:00:00-04:00">July 23, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>756. Local press announces that Condor Airline<anchor n="31" xml:id="d354-f1"/>
                    will inaugurate second weekly service between Buenos Aires and Santiago
                    beginning July 24. Westbound schedules Mondays and Thursdays; eastbound
                    Wednesdays and Saturdays all will stop at Mendoza.</p>
                <p>Panagra<anchor n="32" xml:id="d354-f2"/> has also been anxious to add another
                    service to Santiago but has been handicapped by scarcity of planes and
                    pilots.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tuck</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d354-f1" n="31" xml:id="d354-f1-content">
                <p>Sindicato Condor Ltda., nominally a Brazilian company.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d354-f2" n="32" xml:id="d354-f2-content">
                <p>Pan American-Grace Airways. 1</p>
            </note>
